 assuming that the unhoused are a  collection of drug addicts criminals  who've chosen this life for themselves  instead of people suffering the  inevitable consequences of gutted social  programs and a nationwide divestment  from affordable housing aiden pretty  serious talk for a comedian  that's right you know john oliver does  this he's obviously a very funny  comedian but on his hbo show which airs  on sunday nights he'll often do deep  dives into pretty serious and meaty  policy uh stuff uh this week was the  homelessness crisis in the united states  which i thought did a really good job of  breaking down not just the obvious  details of the crisis but also how we  perceive the homeless and how media  covers them um i think one thing that  gets lost in this debate about  homelessness and the crisis in the  united states um is that we often  descend into sort of culture war uh  fights about this um you know fox news  for example will cover homelessness as  this sort of evil plague on cities like  san francisco a plague that exists  because of feeble liberal governance um  so i think taking a step back and  looking at the crisis and trying to  figure out a way that we can address it  whilst treating homelessness like a  problem for the people that are actually  suffering for it uh is something that's  worth doing and that's something that  john oliver really drilled home  so i thought it was a great uh really  great episode of his show on sunday  night in aidan for the loser you chose  the white house correspondent for the  news max network tell us about emerald  robinson  that's right so emerald robinson is the  white house correspondent for newsmax um  she claimed on twitter uh this week in a  tweet that has now since been removed um  that vaccines contain some sort of  satanic tracker um called luciferase  and it's this really dumb conspiracy  theory that we traced back um it's been  bouncing around the internet for months  reuters actually fact checked it a 